::U1P01::Which statement best reflects multidimensional wellness? {=Physical, mental, emotional, social, and environmental factors can interact ~Only physical fitness matters ~Appearance proves health ~Health never changes}

::U1P02::Which is an external health influence? {=Media messaging ~Personal value ~Private attitude ~Individual priority}

::U1P03::Which goal is measurable? {=Walk 15 minutes on four days each week for three weeks ~Exercise more ~Become healthier ~Try when possible}

::U1P04::A student has poor sleep, low concentration, and irritability. What is the best inference? {=Several wellness dimensions may be interacting ~Only social health is involved ~Appearance caused the problem ~No dimensions interact}

::U1P05::Which monitoring method matches a three-days-per-week activity goal? {=A dated activity-frequency log ~A list of favorite foods ~A general opinion ~An equipment photograph}

::U1P06::What should a student do when lightning threatens an outdoor activity? {=Postpone, relocate safely, or seek appropriate guidance ~Continue at maximum speed ~Ignore it ~Use broken indoor equipment}

::U1P07::What is the strongest first step in a health decision? {=Identify the decision and relevant facts ~Act impulsively ~Ignore options ~Choose the popular answer}

::U1P08::A barrier is forgetting shoes. Which strategy best matches it? {=Prepare shoes beside the backpack the night before ~Double activity intensity ~Remove the deadline ~Track mood only}

::U1P09::Which response is appropriate for a serious warning sign during activity? {=Stop and seek appropriate assistance ~Push through it ~Increase difficulty ~Hide it}

::U1P10::Which plan is most complete? {=SMART goal, safe action, barrier strategy, matching monitoring, support, and adjustment rule ~A vague wish ~An unsafe challenge ~A goal with no evidence}

